{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5418) from a code generation pipeline for the go-unix-utils project. The task requires implementing `cmd/expr` — the Unix `expr` utility in Go — specifically SRD requirements R1.1 through R1.4 covering arithmetic operators, comparison operators, logical operators, and parentheses grouping. Two files must be created: `cmd/expr/main.go` (implementation) and `cmd/expr/expr_test.go` (differential tests against `gexpr`). Acceptance criteria require successful build, vet, and test passes.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Recursive descent expression parser with operator precedence\n   - GNU expr semantics: each token (operator, operand, parenthesis) is a separate command-line argument\n   - Operator precedence (lowest to highest): `|`, `&`, comparisons (`< <= = != >= >`), `+ -` (arithmetic), `* / %`\n   - Left-associative binary operators\n   - Numeric vs lexicographic comparison (if both operands parse as integers, compare numerically; otherwise lexicographically)\n   - Logical operators: `|` returns first arg if nonzero/non-empty, else second; `&` returns first if both nonzero/non-empty, else 0\n   - Exit codes: 0 (non-null/non-zero result), 1 (null/zero result), 2 (syntax error/division by zero), 3 (internal error)\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` against Homebrew `gexpr`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - String operations (match, substr, index, length) from R2 are NOT in this task's scope but may be needed for a complete implementation\n   - `+ TOKEN` escaping from R3.1 is NOT in this task's scope\n   - Division by zero must print error to stderr and exit 2\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd066-expr.yaml` (READ)\n      - Contains full SRD for expr utility with 4 requirement groups (R1-R4)\n      - R1.1: arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /, %) — each operator/operand is a separate argument\n      - R1.2: comparison operators (<, <=, =, !=, >=, >) — numeric comparison if both are integers, else lexicographic; returns \"1\" for true, \"0\" for false\n      - R1.3: logical operators (| for or, & for and) with specific short-circuit semantics\n      - R1.4: parentheses `(` and `)` as separate arguments for grouping\n      - R3.2: precedence order (lowest to highest): |, &, comparisons, +/-, */%\n      - R3.3: all binary operators are left-associative\n      - R3.4: division by zero → stderr error, exit 2\n      - R4.1-R4.3: exit code semantics (0=truthy, 1=falsy, 2=syntax error, 3=internal)\n      - Non-goals: no --help/--version, no arbitrary precision, no ERE (only BRE with \\( \\))\n   \n   - `cmd/expr/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n      - expr implementation with expression parser\n      - Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main()\n   \n   - `cmd/expr/expr_test.go` (TO CREATE)\n      - Differential tests using `testutils.RunDiffTests` with `gexpr` reference binary\n      - Must use `exec.LookPath(\"gexpr\")` with `t.Skip` if not found\n\n   - Existing pkg/ code patterns (provided inline in prompt):\n      - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`: `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` pattern\n      - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go`: `DiffTest` struct, `RunDiffTests`, `BuildBinary`\n      - `pkg/testutils/build.go`: `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles cmd/ package\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only one file was read before summarization was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full specification for expr\n   - Identified that while the task specifies only R1.1-R1.4, a working implementation requires the precedence rules from R3.2-R3.3 and exit code semantics from R4.1-R4.3 as foundational infras